.TH wx-where 1  "where " 
.SH NAME
wx\-where \- The National Weather Service office, grid, zones and nearest stations for a place
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwx where\fR [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-stations\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPLACE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
The National Weather Service office, grid, zones and nearest stations for a place
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-stations\fR \fI<STATIONS>\fR [default: 5]
Number of nearby observation stations to list
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPLACE\fR>
A station (KSJC), latitude,longitude, NWS grid square (MTR 99,82) or zone (CAZ513), US street address or place name ("Mountain View, CA"); quotes are optional
